{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":62088,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"97c05628-7a94-545d-ad08-c26112234512","total_cost_usd":0.275353,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12650,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5566,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12650,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5566,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12650},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9598,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009693,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5566,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12650,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.26566,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:stage1-recovery-claude-05\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated scientific task is explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen, so the screened subset is the intended target, not the complete scheduled network.\",\"observed_value\":\"conditional target\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report declares the target population as the 72 signal-eligible stations, matching the conditional task rather than the 96-station network.\",\"observed_value\":72,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result is explicitly scoped to signal-eligible stations and uses the matching 72-station denominator, so numerator and denominator share the same conditional domain.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/72 = 25%\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow constructs the selected line with the eligible-station denominator and an explicit 'Among signal-eligible stations' qualifier, so the code does not generalize the rate to the full network.\",\"observed_value\":\"SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS denominator\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"RESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Strongest evidence toward the in-scope issue: a larger scheduled network of 96 stations exists and is reported, so a complete-domain denominator of 96 was available and was not used.\",\"observed_value\":96,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input data records 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set that were never assessed, the excluded mass that a complete-domain rate would have to carry.\",\"observed_value\":24,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"outside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to establish the retained-subset-for-complete-domain mismatch by testing whether any stated task or reported claim requires the full 96-station scheduled network. The task line asks for a rate 'conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen'; the report's target line names the 72 eligible stations; and the selected-result sentence is scope-qualified as 'Among signal-eligible stations'. The 96-station network appears only as descriptive context and in the planned-unit accounting line, never as the claim's domain. No sentence generalizes 25% to the scheduled network, so the attempted demonstration fails and the exception for a target explicitly conditional on the retained subset applies.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated task requires a rate for the entire scheduled survey network (complete domain).\",\"observed_value\":\"entire scheduled network\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result uses the complete 96-station scheduled denominator, matching the stated complete-domain target, rather than the 72 retained stations.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/96 = 0.1875\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":15,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report states the exposure denominator explicitly as all 96 scheduled stations, with the 24 omitted stations retained in the denominator contributing zero occurrences.\",\"observed_value\":96,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":14,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow code divides by SCHEDULED_STATIONS-labeled 96 in the selected line, so the emitted denominator is the complete domain, and no screened-subset rate is emitted anywhere in the report text.\",\"observed_value\":\"SCHEDULED_STATIONS denominator\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF\"}]},{\"description\":\"Data supports the counts used: 96 station rows, of which 24 are screen-omitted with NA occurrence flags, e.g. the final omitted row.\",\"observed_value\":\"omitted rows carry NA\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":97,\"end_line\":97,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Strongest evidence toward the in-scope issue: the numerator of 18 occurrences is observed only among the 72 retained stations, so the complete-domain rate imputes zero occurrences for unobserved units; the report labels this a lower bound rather than a retained-subset rate.\",\"observed_value\":18,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report explicitly disclaims any screened-subset claim, which falsifies the hypothesis that a retained-subset denominator underlies any reported rate.\",\"observed_value\":\"no subset rate reported\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":19,\"quoted_text\":\"The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\\nNo screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I searched every emitted report line and every workflow string for a selected or supporting rate whose denominator equals the retained count of 72 while the claim scope is the full network. The only rate emitted is 18/96, the denominator sentence names all 96 scheduled stations, and the limitations section explicitly states no screened-subset rate is reported. I also checked whether the 72 value is used arithmetically in analysis.py; it appears only in the descriptive PASSED_LINE (L0018), never as a divisor. The in-scope mismatch therefore cannot be demonstrated.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"bounded_statement\":\"The selected result is labeled as the occurrence rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network' yet divides the 18 occurrences by the 72 screen-retained stations instead of the 96 scheduled stations declared as the target population, so the reported 0.25 rate uses a retained-subset exposure denominator for a claim that requires the complete 96-station domain.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow hard-codes SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72) as the divisor in the selected-result line while the target and claim text assert the complete scheduled network (96); the 24 screen-omitted stations, which carry NA occurrence flags in the input, are silently dropped from the exposure denominator rather than retained as unobserved scheduled units.\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated task requires one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network, i.e. the complete domain.\",\"observed_value\":\"entire scheduled survey network\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report declares the target population as all 96 scheduled stations, not a screened subset.\",\"observed_value\":96,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result claims network-wide scope but uses the 72 retained stations as the exposure denominator, dropping the 24 omitted scheduled stations.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/72 = 0.25\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow code hard-codes SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS as the divisor while the sentence asserts entire-network scope, confirming the mismatch is produced by the analysis, not a formatting artifact.\",\"observed_value\":\"SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS divisor\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input data shows all 96 rows are scheduled='yes'; the 24 excluded rows are excluded only by screen_status='omitted' and carry NA occurrence flags, so they are in-domain scheduled units with unobserved outcomes.\",\"observed_value\":\"scheduled yes, omitted, NA\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Falsification attempt evidence: the report transparently discloses the retained denominator and the 24 omitted stations, which could be read as making the estimate conditional; however the selected-result sentence still asserts entire-network scope, so disclosure does not restate the target as conditional.\",\"observed_value\":\"24 omitted disclosed\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Stations omitted by the signal screen: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report states no protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists, removing any documented authorization to redefine the target as the retained subset.\",\"observed_value\":\"no amendment\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to falsify the mismatch by looking for any statement that redefines the scientific target as the screened subset, which would place the case under the explicit conditional-target exception. The task line demands a rate for 'the entire scheduled survey network'; the report's target line names all 96 scheduled stations; the selected-result sentence itself repeats 'for the entire scheduled survey network'; and the protocol-status line denies any amendment or approved deviation. I also tested whether the omitted 24 rows might be out of domain, but every such row records scheduled='yes' with screen_status='omitted' and occurrence_flag=NA, i.e. in-domain but unobserved. No conditional restatement exists, so the falsification attempt fails and the complete-domain requirement stands against a 72-station denominator.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":13368,"ttft_stream_ms":1768,"time_to_request_ms":9,"type":"result","duration_ms":61546,"uuid":"c7479dbd-5d4a-4256-a422-db93ab7212aa"}
